```java
while (sc.hasNextLine()) {
    String line = sc.nextLine().strip();
    if (line.isBlank()) {
        continue;
    }
    System.out.println(line);
}
```

Always check `hasNext...` before reading when the amount is unknown. Calling `nextInt()` with nothing left throws `NoSuchElementException`.

example.code:
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int[] scores = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            scores[i] = sc.nextInt();
        }

        int max = scores[0];
        int total = 0;
        for (int s : scores) {
            max = Math.max(max, s);
            total += s;
        }
        System.out.println("Max: " + max);
        System.out.printf("Average: %.2f%n", (double) total / n);

        int bonus = 0;
        while (sc.hasNextInt()) {
            bonus += sc.nextInt();
        }
        System.out.println("Bonus: " + bonus);
    }
}

